        "create_time": 1778567124.821,
        "update_time": 1778567131.782676,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "翻译：\"\"Preregistered validity battery: To test whether matched\r\ncontrol conclusions are operator-artifacts rather than pathway\r\nspecific signal use, we conducted an 8-run confirmatory bat\r\ntery with preregistered hypotheses, endpoints, and pass/fail\r\ncriteria (see Supplement for full preregistration block). Pri\r\nmary: ResNet; Sentinel: SE-ResNet. Disease-pathway pairs:\r\nCLBBB/QRS (expected positive specificity) and 1AVB/PR\r\n(expected non-specific). Three operators: zero-masking, lin\r\near interpolation (continuity-preserving), and beat-conditioned\r\ninpainting (amplitude-aligned adjacent-beat replacement). Ad\r\nditional dimensions: dose-response (40/80/160/240 ms), lead\r\nlocal specificity (precordial V1/V2/V6 vs limb leads). All runs\r\nuse identical matched positive/negative subsets and patient\r\nlevel bootstrap CIs (1,000 iterations). The preregistered pri\r\nmary endpoint requires ASS> 0 with CI lower bound > 0 for\r\n≥2of 3 operators (CLBBB) and ASS≤ 0 with CI upper bound\r\n≤0for ≥2of3operators (1AVB). Secondary endpoints: dose\r\nresponse monotonicity and lead-local specificity.\"\""
          ]
        },
